{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502848-when-a-rite-calls-out-a-particular-fera-in-text-does-it-mean-that-fera-exclusively","id":1502848,"title":"When a Rite calls out a particular Fera in text, does it mean that Fera exclusively?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-12T10:10:30-08:00","id":1502848,"title":"When a Rite calls out a particular Fera in text, does it mean that Fera exclusively?","content":"For instance I get the impression the Rite of the Bolt Hole, which Ratkin use to tunnel into the umbra, or long distances in the real world via the umbra, means that only Ratkin can use or benefit from it when it mentions Ratkin in its text. It even says only Ratkin can use the tunnels. Then again they have a Rite of Dedication where you temporarily bond a group of Ratkin to a patron spirit - how do people feel about such Rites being attempted with a mixed group? Harder? Spirits seem offended or curious? Rite fails? You need to adjust the Rite accordingly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T10:23:43-08:00","id":1502852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502848-when-a-rite-calls-out-a-particular-fera-in-text-does-it-mean-that-fera-exclusively#post1502848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance I get the impression the Rite of the Bolt Hole, which Ratkin use to tunnel into the umbra, or long distances in the real world via the umbra, means that only Ratkin can use or benefit from it when it mentions Ratkin in its text. It even says only Ratkin can use the tunnels. Then again they have a Rite of Dedication where you temporarily bond a group of Ratkin to a patron spirit - how do people feel about such Rites being attempted with a mixed group? Harder? Spirits seem offended or curious? Rite fails? You need to adjust the Rite accordingly?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rat is a Bone Gnawer totem just for an example, so unless it's called out as exclusive to a certain brand of Fera for anatomic/symbolic/thematic reasons, i see no reason to block access to a ritual if some Garou or other fera have a connection to a totem or individual spirit of the appropriate sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T10:28:23-08:00","id":1502855,"title":"","content":"I usually treat Rites as secrets and that they need to be empowered by the spirits who are enabling them. That means that the Rites only work for those who have made the pacts with the spirits for them to work. This means that many may not work for other breeds or sometimes just other tribes without exploration, tinkering and possibly a pact with spirits.<br /> <br /> Others may be simpler and more straightforward doing simple tasks with common spirits, I'd be more lenient about those and letting them just be learned with the right tutoring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T12:02:31-08:00","id":1502861,"title":"","content":"Some rites seem to be fairly universal and others seem to be specific for one group of beings (Fera, breed, tribe, camp, etc.). <br /> <br /> I'll also note here that while in the sourcebooks the various rites are written in a strict game mechanic way, that the flavor text heavily implies that one group's &quot;Rite of whatever&quot; is in fact different from other groups, hence the need to always roll Rituals. All Garou can theoretically access the Rite of Summoning for example, but how a Fenrir performs the rite is different from a Fianna or a Shadow Lord or Black Fury etc. even though its the same rite mechanically.<br /> <br /> I don't think there are any hard and fast rules that helps an ST decide whether this rite mentioned for this Fera should or should not be available to others. I do think STs should make the distinction that certain rites should be excluded for certain groups or allowed in others, but what that is should be left to the ST. In short, if you think it is appropriate, do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T13:24:34-08:00","id":1502871,"title":"","content":"You might be able to have Garou use them, but then they'd have trouble contending with the Ratkin and BSDs that are the more typical user of tunnels, just like how there would be uncomfortable consequences, to say the least, if a Corax tried to just up and use Rite of the Silver Pack for their own purposes, per their own breed book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}